  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Green Deal Knowledge Hub Climate - Provisional title</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Green Deal Knowledge Hub Climate - Provisional title - This action supports a new Phase of the Green Deal Knowledge Hub and the provision of services through 3 technical assistance Facilities respectively on sustainable energy; climate action; and on the integration (or mainstreaming) of environment, climate change, biodiversity and Disaster Risk Reduction in EU action.These Facilities will support the implementation of the Global Gateway Strategy and the external dimension of the European Green Deal, with the aim to accelerate the transition towards inclusive low-carbon, resilient and environmentally sustainable development in partner countries,They will provide high-level policy advice and technical assistance to partner countries, at country, regional and global level, relevant knowledge, data, tools, products, solutions gateways and trainings on climate change, sustainable energy, environment, disaster risk reduction, biodiversity, ecosystems services, sustainable food-systems and green economy, to relevant stakeholders including EU colleagues from EUDs and Headquarter.The EU Energy Facility (EUR 27.7 m) will support partner countries in their efforts to create the conditions to improve the access to and generation of affordable, reliable, and sustainable energy solutions, their regulatory frameworks and their market environments.The Nationally Determined Contribution Facility (NDCF) (EUR 14 m) will promote climate action by, amongst others, enhancing update and implementation of partner countries&#xbf; NDCs, Long Term Strategies (LTS), DRR Strategies and National Adaptation Plans (NAPs) in the context of the Paris Agreement, the Sendai Framework and the 2030 Agenda.The Greening Facility (EUR 2 m) will strengthen the integration of environment, biodiversity, DRR and climate change in EU supported policies, programmes and investments.</narrative>
  </description>
